# §4.8's copy-in/copy-out, executed rather than inspected: the callee works on a
# copy, and the copy-out happens on EVERY exit edge — including the early return
# below, which is the sentence panel 000 named as the place this project would
# stall. `seen` must be 3 after the call, not 0.
#
# Both arguments are named, because two of the parameters share a type (§4.9's
# same-typed-argument rule) — the marker and the label sit together: `n: @n`.
# Bulk regression case.

function count_down(@n: int, @seen: int)
    while n > 0
        seen @ seen + 1
        n @ n - 1
        if seen > 2
            return

function main()
    n: int @ 10
    seen: int @ 0
    count_down(n: @n, seen: @seen)
    print(n)
    print(seen)
